that you're going to need in  moments of deep deep need so  there is the back and forth of the  urgent and the long term  but i think if you're good in leadership  you always tie those two things together  think about the urgency of this year  we built um in c40 a covet 19  recovery playbook with these mayors from  around the world a committee that i  constituted and the  mayor of milan was the chair of it but  we had an incredible mayor from each  continent write this script and it's all  about the long-term recovery  don't just build back what we had don't  return to normal  that isn't good enough we should be  rejecting fossil fuels as we  build our energy grids back we should  have no stimulus it's not a green  stimulus we should be investing in  public transit  above and beyond what was there before  if we want people to actually  a surge into the economy so what seems  urgent in  the now is really about the long term  visioning as well and i think good  leaders can combine those too  thank you thank you our last student  question is from jessica barzilla  hey jessica hi eric garcetti thank you  so much for  coming to speak to us as a fellow alum  of harvard westlake i wanted to ask you  what lessons you've carried with you  from high school and especially as  the classroom experience has gotten  totally warped and coveted  what do you think a high school  education should do and should be  i think high school education first and  foremost is about  your emotional development i know we  fixate so much on academic and  there's a lot of important academic  development but i've learned you know  be nice figure out people who are nice  to you  be around people that that uh celebrate  you  um rather than kind of denigrate you  um know who you know don't chase the  shiny things that seem shiny at the time  but really  you know my best friends my three best  friends are still my best friends from  seventh grade we did  we did plays together we were all you  know aspiring actors two are still  actors today  and and we hang out to this very day  and i think you know those life lessons  are so much more important than  the i mean i had extraordinary education  i remember many pieces  of that education i think the other  thing is to return to what i said before  is be fearless and try  everything um don't think you know  we all have imposter syndrome women  experience that especially people of  color especially  but you know you can pick you know the  third generation vanderbilt like air  whatever he's doing  you know everybody kind of wonders how  the hell am i here and that's okay  human beings are naturally uh  inquisitive and brave and we're  naturally kind of down on ourselves and  wondering like  whether we can do it or whether we're  frauds and we'll be failures  the other thing i learned was when you  try everything it's okay to fail  um you know in politics that's tough  lesson because if you're an entrepreneur  you can fail four times and if you're  fifth times a hit you are like a legend  in politics you do four things great but  you mess up once  it's done so it's the inverse kind of  leadership uh  reward but if we can bring more  entrepreneurialism and creativity to our  lives and i think that's something that  i learned  certainly in my education the world will  be okay  we are a stubborn people human beings we  are creative people human beings  um there's nothing including climate  change um  racial justice this pandemic that we  can't rise to  the day that i stopped believing in that  is the day i quit being a leader  here at stanford mayor garcia we like to  end with a quick lightning round  uh so one word answers or one sentence  answers are you ready  favorite thing about l.a  freedom most misunderstood thing about  l.a  walking most misunderstood thing about  being mayor  being all powerful tick tock or  instagram  heart tick tock daily practice instagram  you have to go away on an extended  vacation  and name one hollywood celebrity as  interim mayor  who do you turn to jimmy kimmel you do a  great job  i agree completely um  we know there's a lot of traffic despite  the walking comment in la what's mayor  garcetti listening to  in his car um  a little bit of everything often keith  jarrett my favorite i'm a pianist i have  a piano in my  office and he's he's the greatest and i  was very sad to learn he just recently  had a stroke and we'll never probably  play again  you have to be mayor of one city outside  of the us  which do you choose barcelona it's where  i got engaged and i love that city  awesome mayor garcia i know you have a  city to run thank you for  for joining us hopefully we can host you  here in person soon i would love that  and thank you so much rex and  and thank you to dean levin to all the  questions they were superb i really  enjoyed the conversation  and i sign off every night when i  address people this way but sending  everybody strength and love  look after your your mental your  spiritual well-being in a really tough  year  and we're gonna get through this  [Music]

